      "wins_if": "it finds m0 != m1 in one domain whose challenge maps are EQUAL, so the difference map D is identically zero and the extractor cannot solve for s",
      "attack": "birthday search over messages",
      "v1.46_output_length": "h = n  (a single challenge c; D(s) = (c0+c1)s)",
      "v1.50_output_length": "h = 3n (the triple; D(s) = a s + b s^2 + c s^4)",
      "lemma": "D is a linearized polynomial of 2-degree <= 2, so its kernel has dimension <= 2 and a PARTIAL collision leaves at most 4 candidate openings, all filtered by the registry. Only a full collision wins.",
      "theory": "Q = sqrt(pi/2 * 2^h); slope 0.5 per bit of h"
